Let's plug $\blueD{a=0}$, $\maroonD{b=5}$, and $\purpleC{g(x)=4\cos\left(\sqrt{x^2+x+5}\right)}$ into the formula:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{\displaystyle\int_{\blueD a}^{\maroonD b} \purpleC{g(x)}\,dx}{\maroonD b-\blueD a}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\displaystyle\int_{\blueD {0}}^{\maroonD 5} \purpleC{4\cos\left(\sqrt{x^2+x+5}\right)}\,dx}{\maroonD 5-\blueD{0}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac15\displaystyle\int_{0}^{5} 4\cos\left(\sqrt{x^2+x+5}\right)\,dx
\end{align}$
